        "text": "Since 1790, the Constitution has required that the census be conducted by an actual enumeration of the population."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Thomas R. Lee, Esq.",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3e34a1134a68630cd60843abd91cdc687d7325c4b75f203b65186dc91b5d8c65",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3e34a1134a68-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The 2000 Census used statistical imputation, adding .4\u202f% (about 1.2\u202fmillion people) by estimating occupants for 620,000 addresses based on neighboring households."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Dellinger",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3e34a1134a68630cd60843abd91cdc687d7325c4b75f203b65186dc91b5d8c65",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3e34a1134a68-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Dellinger, utah contends that this imputation violates the constitutional requirement for an actual count."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg and Justice O'Connor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3e34a1134a68630cd60843abd91cdc687d7325c4b75f203b65186dc91b5d8c65",
            "evidence_ids": [
